==Spanish==

===Etymology===
{{unk.|es}}, maybe related to French {{m|fr|gai}}, Italian {{m|it|gaio}}, English {{m|en|gay}} of Germanic origin or from Arabic {{m|ar|كويس||tr=kuwayyis}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈɡwaj/|lang=es}}

===Adjective===
{{es-adj|pl=guais}}
{{es-adj-inv}}

# {{lb|es|Spain|slang}} [[cool]]

====Usage notes====
* This adjective is most often treated as invariable, with the form {{m|es||guay}} being used regardless of gender or number; however, the plural form {{m|es|guais}} is also often found. Hence, “They're very cool” may be expressed either as ''son muy guay'' or as ''son muy guays''.

===Adverb===
{{es-adv}}

# {{lb|es|Spain|slang}} [[cool]]

